{"path":"experimental/simd/simd_cast","title":"std::experimental::simd_cast, std::experimental::static_simd_cast","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::</span>simd_cast, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::</span>static_simd_cast","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/simd/simd_cast","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Cast a simd object to another simd object. If V is T, returns simd<T, Abi>; otherwise, if V is a scalar type, returns simd<V, simd_abi::fixed_size<simd<T, Abi>::size()>>.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/simd\">&lt;experimental/simd&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-parallelism_ts_2\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> V, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Abi <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*see below*/</span> simd_cast<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> simd<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, Abi<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> v <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-parallelism-ts-2 t-mark-ts\">(parallelism TS v2)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-parallelism_ts_2\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> V, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Abi <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*see below*/</span> static_simd_cast<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> simd<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, Abi<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> v <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-parallelism-ts-2 t-mark-ts\">(parallelism TS v2)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Cast a simd object to another simd object. If V is T, returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">simd<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, Abi<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code>; otherwise, if V is a scalar type, returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">simd<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V, simd_abi<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">fixed_size</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>simd<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, Abi<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span></span></code>. Otherwise, V must be a simd type, and the function returns V.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> This function does not participate in overloading resolution unless\n<ul><li> every possible value of the input element can be represented with the output element,\n</li><li> either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">is_simd_v<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is false, or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">V<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">simd<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, Abi<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> This function does not participate in overloading resolution unless either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">is_simd_v<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is false, or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">V<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">simd<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, Abi<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> v\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the input simd object\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A simd object with the i-th element initialized to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">static_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>To<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v<span class=\"br0\">[</span>i<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, where To is the output element type as specified.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The TS specification is missing <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">simd_cast</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">static_simd_cast</span></code> overloads for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">simd_mask</span></code>. The libstdc++ implementation provides the missing overloads in the <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span>__proposed</span></code> namespace. If you already use the\n</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> stdx <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></code></pre>\n<p>shortcut, you might be interested to use\n</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> stdx <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span>__proposed<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>instead. Alternatively, libstdc++ implements a <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">__cvt<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> member function in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">simd_mask</span></code>, which allows implicit conversion of the mask. See also: <a class=\"external free\" href=\"https://github.com/VcDevel/std-simd/issues/41\" data-external=\"1\">https://github.com/VcDevel/std-simd/issues/41</a>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/simd","title":"SIMD library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::simd_cast, std::experimental::static_simd_cast","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Cast a simd object to another simd object."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"v"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A simd object with the i-th element initialized to static_cast<To>(v[i]), where To is the output element type as specified."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The TS specification is missing simd_cast and static_simd_cast overloads for simd_mask."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":238,"codeBlockCount":2}
